  <HOMEWORK title="PLL Bring-Up 2: Closing the loop - to the wrong frequency"
            prompt="The VCO's free-run frequency is now close to spec, so the loop filter is connected for the first time. Status reports LOCKED almost immediately. Before moving on, confirm the thing that actually matters: is the output frequency the right one?"
            hint="Read the VCO output frequency directly and compare it against reference x the programmed feedback divider. Does the divider actually match what this board is specified to use?"
            explanation="The feedback divider is programmed for N=41 instead of the specified N=40, so the now-closed loop locks exactly as designed - just to 25 MHz x 41 = 1025 MHz instead of the intended 1000 MHz. A solid LOCKED status only confirms the loop found a stable, phase-aligned state; it says nothing about whether that state is the one you wanted (HOMEWORK_26 demonstrates the same fault in isolation). Always cross-check the actual output frequency against reference x N before trusting a freshly-closed loop's lock indicator. The fix is correcting the feedback divider to the specified N=40."/>
</LABCHAIN>
